#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119526 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/id #uuid "4efedc4e-19e9-552c-bc27-814df953e141" :question/math-academy-id "e-4575" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpress $y$ in terms of $2 \\times 2$ determinants." :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y=-1 \\\\ -3x+3y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_y$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119528 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "311ba12f-de22-580c-9e0d-6766f7864d1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4578" :question/problem "Let $\\langle x,3 \\rangle$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=4 \\\\ x+ky=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/b82f5c43c9ec788b95e7213bef63eb37e4abf9d0159f92cbeedc0f64c4d35283.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/648ce0c1b8b77c1230c6c634c676624f9c79c12ffc3942abc09d24d0fdc424d3.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/bc7a566778813050611b098cebe221aa77ac27677e922cd282fc8ff9c3670cfd.png)" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\dfrac{D_y}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot 8-4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{36}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}| & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119585 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "d81e32a1-bd93-5a95-bb4a-e8df9063b5aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-5230" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057622/assets/2d3571405367c6d4ce15927a1dbdb50a30af7d13580c7b9cd3c73bada0583c98.png)\nExpress $D_x$ in terms of a $2 \\times 2$ determinant." :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ 2x+y=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_x$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b698822-324b-5a2a-b201-40054afc1568" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335077} {:answer/id #uuid "6899dc1a-2662-5d3e-a868-8805c0f3a4bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335078} {:answer/id #uuid "85e33954-33ed-5008-aec1-aa1f1259f3ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 17\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335079} {:answer/id #uuid "af0453aa-99b8-56ca-898c-ad63d492aa5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 2 \\\\ 13 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335080} {:answer/id #uuid "5640075d-cf38-587f-b6e7-b3f1bd03fd08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 2 \\\\ 13 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b698822-324b-5a2a-b201-40054afc1568" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335077} :answer-field/id #uuid "e22a3cf1-0e45-55ec-bf4a-355272f9dd76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3dee3a3d-b589-52d5-8b29-2264540bb947" :question/math-academy-id "q-139960" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y=-14 \\\\ 5x+4y=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y=-14 \\\\ 5x+4y=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & -14 \\\\ 5 & 13\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a6625a9-0cbb-5d69-831e-42ed9c34b8f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335097} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b03701-9bf7-5704-9400-efc75b897a63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335098} {:answer/id #uuid "e4bbd7c9-8930-5ee8-bc6f-5f7a8c019383" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335099} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6a0891-e60b-5a38-84db-bdc915719ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,3 & 15 \\\\ -2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335100} {:answer/id #uuid "eb2c8935-3dfc-5612-a3f6-4aecbcf5bbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb2c8935-3dfc-5612-a3f6-4aecbcf5bbf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335101} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d53fa8d-1654-53d1-9a47-803744d17efb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c2e31ac-502a-53cd-a44d-a0ec535a4195" :question/math-academy-id "q-42606" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y=15 \\\\ 2x-3y=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y=15 \\\\ 2x-3y=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -9\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335109 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271c346f-48e5-5989-931c-c9f3fb5caab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335111} {:answer/id #uuid "07927c49-daa6-599c-99a3-151ad9664a0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335112} {:answer/id #uuid "58786e39-375f-5c88-bf3b-57b71a14ddb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335113} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5cbc82-821d-546d-9470-35ee16eaaa68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335114} {:answer/id #uuid "5e40c96e-c9bd-5724-8916-6682b2018ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58786e39-375f-5c88-bf3b-57b71a14ddb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335113} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c1d2ba-bbf2-5aca-8c0c-7c5e798319ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff9ce129-3900-5770-b561-66ce2c4a5268" :question/math-academy-id "q-42613" :question/problem "Let $⟨-4,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9x+11y=-14 \\\\ 6x-ky=-34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=-4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 1 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n- $-4|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ -4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335116 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fcf3704-4856-5095-a6f4-7ec20d81f3c4" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing an Unknown in Terms of 2x2 Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82becbd4-494e-51ec-b394-8bedbea10379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,7 & 13 \\\\ -5 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335118} {:answer/id #uuid "11243639-943e-5bfb-a34c-de52a98d61fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335119} {:answer/id #uuid "c690e8e3-2d8b-51c3-a855-be53aebb7423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,13 & 7 \\\\ 19 & 5\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335120} {:answer/id #uuid "a77f0a77-582f-5eb8-ad33-74421fbbbd46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,2 & 13 \\\\ -4 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335121} {:answer/id #uuid "e2bd768d-2c7d-51c6-8b03-5b63b5110a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}13 & \\,\\,\\,4 \\\\ 19 & -2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11243639-943e-5bfb-a34c-de52a98d61fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335119} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa457e1d-9b2b-5b7c-9211-e5239cbd3fd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69a6ad9d-656e-51bb-9c61-6471ddfbd822" :question/math-academy-id "q-42970" :question/problem "Consider the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+7y=13 \\\\ -2x+5y=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, $y=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+7y=13 \\\\ -2x+5y=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 19\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parts of Cramer's Rule Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75d42042-434d-5a69-aacc-193880c3c2d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335152} {:answer/id #uuid "5506e7ea-4684-502f-a34b-5360e1da77aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335153} {:answer/id #uuid "1c4cff56-39c3-58b0-90a7-952e85dfe6cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335154} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7440b8-7c4a-5380-8837-6cd2205c7b52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335155} {:answer/id #uuid "126916aa-c8be-5d9d-822a-919524a2ad50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c4cff56-39c3-58b0-90a7-952e85dfe6cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335154} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b8c6a4e-1f22-5f7e-b077-0f7db42cd782" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d47b44f-bbb3-54e7-8ca3-2db255852117" :question/math-academy-id "q-70201" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3x-3y=1 \\\\ -x+2y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $y$ can be written as $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}$, where ${D}_{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3x-3y=1 \\\\ -x+2y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$, we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & \\,\\,1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbd05303-f84e-5c67-b25f-01fc8466c943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335159} {:answer/id #uuid "744e467e-bda6-53b3-b523-5d32ebad0211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335160} {:answer/id #uuid "4fbbbcb1-bc09-5aad-a102-41f1f825662b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335161} {:answer/id #uuid "3791b02d-ebb5-586f-a80d-c9c0f6c0d972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335162} {:answer/id #uuid "4330df1e-c834-580d-9cec-35670e81873f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fbbbcb1-bc09-5aad-a102-41f1f825662b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335161} :answer-field/id #uuid "37292bee-6ead-58b3-9354-c6080811ad1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "745a2d2f-9203-593c-9a03-87c0afb1d76b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70252" :question/problem "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+ky=-4 \\\\ 3x-4y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}]}
